# Rust / Tauri

- New IPC: `src-tauri/src/commands/<domain>.rs`, `mod.rs`, then `main.rs` handler.
- Keep commands thin at the edge; heavy decode/hash/IO in Rust (`spawn_blocking`).
- Pass paths across IPC, not image buffers.
- Prefer existing Tauri plugins over custom commands when they already fit.
- Reuse helpers in `commands/` (e.g. oriented image decode).
- Return `Result` at the command boundary; don’t unwrap user-facing IO.
